course: dictionary
lesson: 4344
title: The word guest
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A guest is a person who is invited. You can be a guest at someone's home, at a party, or at an event. You can also be a guest at a hotel, where you stay for a few nights. Read the words around guest to find out which meaning fits. «The hotel had a guest room for visiting family.» Here guest means a person staying at the hotel.
explain: The clues tell you who the guest is and why they are there. In the Wonderland procession, «the guests» walk along hand in hand with the soldiers, courtiers and royal children, so they are people invited to the event, not people who work there. Ask yourself: who is coming, and why? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: «Be my guest» is a phrase, so do not translate it word by word. It means «go ahead, help yourself». If a friend says «Be my guest» when you ask to use their pencil, you can take it.
explain: In Bradford, Hamid goes to a wedding with 300 guests, and about 20 aunties pinch his cheeks: «Mashallah, so big now!» Mashallah is said to admire something good, and means roughly «God has willed it». Words from other languages carry feelings too, and the context shows you what they mean.
fact: A guest is a person who is invited to your home, a party or an event.
fact: A guest can also be a person staying at a hotel.
fact: A guest on a show is a visitor who comes to talk or perform.
fact: «Be my guest» means «go ahead, help yourself».
fact: Useful phrases with guest include «guest room», «guest list» and «special guest».
exercise: In the Wonderland procession, «the guests» jump along hand in hand. Who are the guests? | The Knave of Hearts | The soldiers carrying clubs | *People invited to the event | The King's cook
exercise: A friend says «Be my guest» when you ask to use their pencil. What does it mean? | *Go ahead, help yourself | Please pay me back later | Be quiet about it | You must leave now
exercise: Mum says, «We have a special guest on the show tonight.» What is a guest on a show? | A helper who sets up the lights | *A visitor who comes to talk or perform | A person who stays in a hotel | A person who cooks the food
test: A sign at the hotel says «Guest room 12». What does guest mean here? | *A room for people staying at the hotel | A room for the staff only | A room for the swimming pool | A room with a kitchen
test: Aunt Sara is writing down who is coming to her wedding. What is the name for this list? | Guest room | Special guest | *Guest list | Guest voice
exam: At a Galway hotel wedding, a person whispers «about time, they've been together for years». What is this person? | *Someone invited to the wedding | The bride | A bridesmaid | The hotel cleaner
